</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation on GSM8K and HumanEval dataset</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the model capacity on reasoning tasks, we also conduct an experiment on the GSM8K (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al. (2021)</a></cite>) and HumanEval (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. (2021)</a></cite>) dataset, with the Llama-3.2-3B model. We keep the hyperparameters as in the main experiments. For the HumanEval dataset, the model is trained on the CodeAlpaca (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chaudhary (2023)</a></cite>) dataset. The Evalscope framework is adopted for evaluation. The results in Tab. <a href="#S4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Evaluation on GSM8K and HumanEval dataset ‣ 4.4 Ablation study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ FURINA: Free from Unmergeable Router via lINear Aggregation of mixed experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> demonstrate that, compared with LoRA, the proposed FURINA could significantly boost the model performance, indicating its generalization capacity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Comparison of LoRA and FURINA on GSM8K and HumanEval datasets </figcaption>
